    {
      "id": "effects-versus-geometry-modifiers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Effects versus geometry modifiers"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "PathEffect modifies stroke shading, opacity, patterns and width profiles. FillEffect modifies interior shading using local coordinates. A path modifier changes contour geometry before it is rendered. A shader dash hides parts of an existing stroke; a geometric dash modifier changes the evaluated path. Choose according to whether downstream sampling and boolean operations should see the altered geometry."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "strokeShader and fillShader accept effect objects, raw WGSL strings or ordered arrays. Effects compile into named helper stages, with output from one stage passed to the next. The order matters for tint, opacity, glow, gradients and custom functions."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Exact contracts: [PathEffect](/api-material#patheffect), [FillEffect](/api-material#filleffect), [PathEffectBase](/api-material#patheffectbase), [FillEffectBase](/api-material#filleffectbase)."
        }
      ]
    },
